  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PER Basket Fund</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">PER Basket Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective for the basket fund was to finance important analytical work on public finance management to identify both progress and weaknesses and thus help the government and development partners to design and prioritise further PFM reform.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Genom korgfonden f&#xf6;r studier om de offentliga finanserna och den offentliga finansiella styrningen (s.k. Public Expenditure Reviews, PER) kommer Sverige bidra till att angel&#xe4;gna studier genomf&#xf6;rs och att v&#xe4;l underbyggda reformer och f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttringar kan implementeras. Urvalet av PER-studier g&#xf6;rs genom en deltagande process som involverar seniora tj&#xe4;nstem&#xe4;n i den tanzaniska statsaparaten s&#xe5;v&#xe4;l som representanter f&#xf6;r civilsamh&#xe4;llet, privatsektorn, bist&#xe5;ndsgivare och en tanzanisk tankesmedja. Insatsen &#xe4;r komplement&#xe4;r till det svenska budgetst&#xf6;det till Tanzania.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the Public Expenditure Review (PER) Basket Fund, Sweden will contribution to critical studies being carried out and that well informed reforms can be implemented. The selection of PER studies is done through a participatory process involving senior government officials as well as representatives from the civil society, private sector, donors and a Tanzanian think-tank. The initiative is complementary to the Swedish budget support operation.</narrative>
  </description>
